FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with ferrion-boot-splash.patch, ferrion-lockdown.patch, ferrion-pty-hangup.patch and ferrion-live-disk-view.patch applied:
- procmgr sends the SIGCHLD a parent gets when its child exits without the permission check of kill(), as POSIX has the system generate that signal. A parent running under another user ID, such as login for a non-root shell, receives it, and the signal still names the child as its sender.
- on_send_sig takes whether to apply that check. The signals a process asks for keep it. The other signals procmgr generates itself (SIGCHLD on stop and continue, SIGCONT and SIGHUP to a newly orphaned process group, SIGCONT and SIGHUP when a controlling terminal is taken over) skip it, which changes nothing for them: they were already sent as init or as the target itself.

